<title>UK: SunAmerica sets 100 bln lire three-year bond.</title>
<headline>SunAmerica sets 100 bln lire three-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Cariplo and Citibank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SUNAMERICA INSTITUTIONAL FUNDING</p>
<p> AMT    100 BLN LIRE  COUPON    *ZERO	MATURITY   *02.JUN.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.275   PAY DATE    02.JUN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.375     LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  =	   DENOMS (K) 500	 SALE LIMITS = US/IT/UK/CY</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.875     SELL CONC  0.50	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES     *REDEMPTION VALUE 100 PCT, PLUS 21.06 PCT PLUS FIVE TIMES</p>
<p>		(10-YEAR ITL SWAP RATE MINUS THREE YEAR ITL SWAP RATE)</p>
<p>		 MINUS 0.44 PCT, SUBJECT TO A MINIMUM COUPON OF ZERO.</p>
<p>		 ISSUED UNDER $500 MLN NOTE ISSUANCE PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
